# NOTE ON PATTERN DEPTH — .dockerignore is NOT .gitignore.
#
# Docker matches each pattern against the file's FULL path relative to the
# build context root, and a pattern segment never spans `/`. So a bare
# `__pycache__/` excludes ONLY `<root>/__pycache__/` — it does nothing about
# `sodamem/memory/__pycache__/`, which would then be copied into the image.
# .gitignore's "match at any depth" behavior does not exist here.
#
# Anything that can appear at more than one level therefore needs an explicit
# `**/` prefix. Getting this wrong is silent: the build still succeeds, it
# just carries files you believed were excluded.

# VCS / editor
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.superpowers/

# Python build/venv/cache artifacts
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info/
**/build/
**/dist/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
.import_linter_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
.coverage.*

# Local data / secrets — never bake these into an image layer
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
data/

# Test suite — not needed in the runtime image
tests/

# JS/TS surfaces and docs. `console/` IS part of the build context — the
# console-builder stage compiles it — but only its source. node_modules is
# reinstalled from the lockfile inside the stage, and a host-built
# `console/dist` must never reach the context: the image ships the dist IT
# built, never a stale local one. Both are covered by the `**/` rules above,
# but `console/dist/` is spelled out anyway because that guarantee is the
# whole reason the console-builder stage exists.
console/dist/
console/node_modules/
sdk-ts/
node_modules/
docs/

# `mcp_server/` is NOT excluded. It is a declared package root, so the
# builder's `uv sync --no-editable` install needs its sources present —
# Dockerfile's `COPY mcp_server ./mcp_server` fails outright without them.
# It was listed here from when the image copied only `server/`, and the
# stale entry survived the change that added the COPY.

# OS cruft
**/.DS_Store

# This project's own Docker build context noise
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.*.yml
